.TH CHANGELOG-BUMP 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog bump \- bump VERSION.txt using environment variables or CI merge request labels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog bump
[\fIlevel\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBbump\fR command automatically updates the project's VERSION.txt file based on bump level indicators from environment variables or CI/CD pipeline labels. It supports semantic versioning (major, minor, patch) and release candidate (rc) versions.

This is designed for integration with continuous integration systems where merge request labels trigger version bumps automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
.B Positional Arguments:
.TP
\fIlevel\fR
Optional bump level specification. Can be provided as positional argument or via environment variables/labels.

Valid levels: major, minor, patch, rc

.TP
.B Optional Flags:
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-level\fR=\fILEVEL\fR
Alias for the positional bump level argument. Allows explicit level specification regardless of environment variables.

.TP
\fB\-\-version-file\fR=\fIPATH\fR
Path to VERSION.txt file to update. Defaults to "VERSION.txt" in current directory. Can specify absolute or relative paths for custom version file locations.
.SH BUMP LEVELS
.PP
The tool supports these version bump levels:

.TP
\fImajor\fR
Increment major version number (X.\fIY\fR.Z → \fIX+1\fR.0.0). Used for breaking changes and incompatible API modifications.

.TP
\fIminor\fR
Increment minor version number (X.Y.\fIZ\fR → X.\fIY+1\fR.0). Used for new features that maintain backward compatibility.

.TP
\fIpatch\fR
Increment patch version number (X.Y.\fIZ\fR → X.Y.\fIZ+1\fR). Used for bug fixes and minor improvements.

.TP
\fIrc\fR
Create release candidate version with incremental counter (X.Y.Z-rc.N → X.Y.Z-rc.\fIN+1\fR). Used for pre-release testing before final version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLE SUPPORT
.PP
The bump command checks these environment variables in order of priority:

.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCHANGELOG_BUMP_LEVEL\fR \- Explicit bump level override
.IP \(bu 2
\fBCI_MERGE_REQUEST_LABELS\fR \- Comma-separated list of CI/CD labels (checks for "bump-major", "bump-minor", "bump-patch")
.IP \(bu 2
\fBGITHUB_EVENT_PATH\fR \- GitHub Actions event payload (extracts labels from merge requests)
.RE

.TP
.B Label Format:
.PP
CI systems should use labels prefixed with "bump-" to trigger version updates:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
"bump-major" → Major version increment
.IP \(bu 2
"bump-minor" → Minor version increment
.IP \(bu 2
"bump-patch" → Patch version increment
.IP \(bu 2
"rc-major", "rc-minor", "rc-patch" → Release candidate versions
.RE

.SH VERSION FILE FORMAT
.PP
VERSION.txt files contain a single line with the current version string:
.nf
    v1.2.3
.fi

.TP
.B After bumping, the file is updated to reflect the new version:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
Major bump (1.2.3 → 2.0.0): "v2.0.0"
.IP \(bu 2
Minor bump (1.2.3 → 1.3.0): "v1.3.0"
.IP \(bu 2
Patch bump (1.2.3 → 1.2.4): "v1.2.4"
.IP \(bu 2
RC version (1.2.3-rc.1 → 1.2.3-rc.2): "v1.2.3-rc.2"
.RE

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Bump patch version using environment variable:
.nf
    export CHANGELOG_BUMP_LEVEL=patch
    changelog bump
.fi

.TP
Explicitly specify major version bump:
.nf
    changelog bump --level major
.fi

.TP
Update custom version file location:
.nf
    changelog bump minor --version-file src/VERSION.txt
.fi

.TP
Create release candidate version (CI/CD integration):
.nf
    # In CI pipeline with label "rc-minor"
    export CI_MERGE_REQUEST_LABELS="rc-minor,needs-review"
    changelog bump
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate release notes after version bumping
.TP
\fBsemver.org\fR \- Semantic Versioning specification reference
